<FeatureFacts id="splits" />

A split is your plan: training days (Push, Pull, Legs, or Monday, Wednesday, Friday), each with its
exercises and sets. One split is **active**; the Today card on Home trains from it.

## Your first plan

The first time you open LogIt it asks three things: what you want from training, how long you've
been lifting, and how many days a week you can train. From those it makes a plan: full body for 2 or
3 days, upper/lower for 4, or upper/lower plus push/pull/legs for 5 or 6, each day on a weekday. On
the plan screen you can say what equipment you have (full gym, home gym, dumbbells only) and how long
a workout can be, and the exercises change to match. Your goal sets each exercise's rep range (for
example 5–8 on the big lifts for "stronger and bigger"), and the days become your weekly target.
It's an ordinary split afterwards: change anything in it, or tap Other plans and then Build my own.

## On the phone

Open Splits, then New. Add days, then open a day to add exercises. Set it active from the split's page.
